## Problem
With Pi 1.0.2 and pi-zentui 0.29.2, `components.userMessages` (enabled, any style, e.g. `labeled`) has no effect: user messages render with Pi's native look. Footer/editor work fine.

## Cause
`nativeMarkdown()` in `extensions/zentui/user-message.ts` only recognises the old `UserMessageComponent` shape: `Container > Box > Markdown` with `paddingX === 0` and `paddingY === 0`. In Pi 1.0.2 `rebuild()` adds the `Markdown` directly (no Box), with `paddingX = outputPad` (1), `paddingY = 1`, and the message background in `defaultTextStyle.bgColor`. The shape check fails, so Zentui silently falls back to the native renderer.

## Suggested fix
- Accept the `Markdown` as a direct child (keep Box-wrapped support for older Pi).
- Drop the zero-padding requirement.
- Strip `bgColor` from the inherited `defaultTextStyle` so the Zentui frame isn't painted over Pi's background.

Working local patch to `nativeMarkdown()`:

```ts
let renderer = children[0];
if (isRecord(renderer) && !isNativeMarkdown(renderer)) {
  const box = renderer;
  if (!Array.isArray(box.children) || box.children.length !== 1) return undefined;
  renderer = box.children[0];
}
if (!isNativeMarkdown(renderer)) return undefined;
const child = renderer as Record<string, unknown>;
if (typeof child.text !== "string" || !isRecord(child.theme)) return undefined;
// ...existing theme/options checks...
const { bgColor: _bg, ...textStyle } = (child.defaultTextStyle ?? {}) as Record<string, unknown>;
// pass `textStyle` (when defaultTextStyle was defined) as input.defaultTextStyle
```

## Environment
- pi-coding-agent 1.0.2, pi-zentui 0.29.2, macOS
- Other components that inspect Pi component internals (e.g. thinking steps) may be affected similarly; not verified.
